hover-preview is inspired by two mods of better-claude (https://github.com/midudev/better-claude):

image-preview and quick-peek
Copyright (c) Miguel Ángel Durán (midudev). MIT License.

What was taken: the idea (hover a pasted [Image #N] or a path in a reply to preview it, click to
open it), the pointer-target pattern of the small Client modules (chip.tsx, link.tsx), the BMP
reading and the linear-light averaging in pixels.ts, and the shape of the path pattern in paths.ts.
What changed: rewritten and much smaller. Terminal only (no macOS, Windows or Tk preview windows,
no kitty graphics), cells drawn with half blocks only, the card is drawn in the band above the
prompt instead of floating over the transcript, paths are shown as a row of links under a reply
block instead of re-laying out the reply's Markdown, and there is no syntax highlighting.

